/**
 * Issue #55: structured sourcing for ingredient-card.js's new Foraged
 * In/Fished From/Dropped By sections (decisions/
 * item-drops-edge-and-item-located-in.md's "method/mobs" section). Adds
 * `item --located_in--> zone` edges tagged `method: "drop"|"forage"|"fish"`
 * (drop edges also carry `mobs`) for every Brewing/Baking ingredient whose
 * own eqlwiki item page states a specific zone via its `dropsfrom`/
 * `foraged` template fields or (fishing only, no structured field exists)
 * a zone named in its free-text `notes`.
 *
 * Batch-fetched directly from eqlwiki.com (raw wikitext, not the free-text
 * `source` field already on many of these items -- see the decision doc
 * for why re-verifying against the wiki won this ingestion, not reusing the
 * existing prose). Ambiguous wiki zone names (bare "Commonlands"/"Kaladim"
 * with no East/West or North/South) and zones not yet catalogued in this
 * graph (Erud's Crossing, Siren's Grotto, Tower of Frozen Shadow,
 * Velketor's Labyrinth, Mines of Nurga) are skipped, same "not catalogued
 * yet" precedent as tradeskill-recipe-node-schema.md's vendor skip list.
 * 3 ingredients have no findable wiki page under their graph label (Gray
 * Ice, Human (Chunk of) Meat, Pondfish Spines) and are absent from DATA
 * entirely -- they keep only their existing free-text `source`.
 *
 * "Crafted In" (the fourth new ingredient-card section) needed no
 * migration at all -- it's the reverse of every recipe's existing
 * `produces` edge, computed at read time by getItemSources() in
 * src/graph.ts.
 */
